  "source_policy": {
    "storage_waiting": "Common helper copies waiting storage to outcome prefix, calls makeFulfilledState with output at +0x18, then installs returned trace and callsite into state and writes fulfilled discriminator 1 at +0x41. Prior waiting storage is returned for downstream dispatch. Callback/trace internals are only partially qualified.",
    "storage_fulfilled": "Branch invokes configured ifAlreadyFulfilled callback and destroys OverfulfillHandle context. On normal no-error return, zeroes the 32-byte outcome, leaving no storage for caller dispatch. Callback throwing/error and OverfulfillHandle cleanup effects are not qualified here.",
    "caller": "Concurrent invalidate passes trace builder through c12c0 and empty callback at 1e5c for already-fulfilled handling. Caller tests returned storage pointer after unlocking and skips both collection loops when absent.",
    "trace": "Forwarder reaches trace builder, which constructs/appends InvalidationTrace.Link values and returns trace storage. It does not itself extract observer collections; the common fulfill helper copies waiting storage. Full link contents/ownership are not mapped.",
    "managed_token": "Void/Void specialization compares state tag at +0x39. Waiting calls makeFulfilledState, installs callsite/tag 1 and writes outcome 0. Fulfilled invokes configured handler, cleans context and on normal no-error return writes outcome 1. Outer caller skips callback for outcome 1, otherwise invokes after unlock.",
    "boundary": "One-shot dispatch suppression is source-qualified for legal tags and normal callback return. No actual repeated native invalidation, concurrency race/reentry, callback delivery, failure-policy behavior or final resource settlement observed."
  },
